+# WD06 stopped — unchanged shared-route E2E conflicts with wire lanes
+
+Attempted on accepted WD05 `acf584ec58adea5c6ebec7ac00711c3153a8311b`.
+This evidence is part of the stopped patch, not a landed implementation. No alternate design,
+old E2E expectation change, board source edit or board test edit was attempted.
+
+## Stop reason
+
+The unchanged `detailed-view.spec.ts` test “Choose relationship offers a relationship once,
+and port marks follow their lines” calls `pointNear` with `cdn-transcoded`,
+`transcoder-write/transcoder-packager` and `transcoder-write/transcoder-thumbnails`. That helper
+requires all three incoming paths within 2 board pixels at the same point. With prescribed
+11px lanes and separate gathered arrowheads there is no such shared run. The full E2E result is:
+`No point where only cdn-transcoded, transcoder-write/transcoder-packager, transcoder-write/transcoder-thumbnails meet.`
+
+Restoring that shared route would contradict the approved distinct lanes/arrowheads; changing
+the old helper/spec would mask the failure. This is the plan’s design-stop boundary. The root
+coordinator independently inspected the unchanged helper and confirmed the conflict. The unit
+therefore saves this binary patch, restores only its own changes, runs the required restored-tree
+gates, appends a stop handoff and commits only the patch and handoff.
+
+## Work tried
+
+Applied the exact Workspace saved-slot assignment/effect, LaneCanvas per-source wire/dot colours
+and `lanes`, Detailed container dot removal, ContainerTile WireTone variables, prescribed theme/
+port/dot CSS, beaded soft-head legend and updated legend test. Added only the two requested E2E
+cases and the prescribed studio/playbook/feedback documentation. The current shape matches the
+brief; Biome import/expression/CSS wrapping was the only mechanical implementation adjustment.
+
+All old E2E source is byte-preserved as a prefix; every board source/test is untouched. A new
+colour/reload case initially read Simple IDs while the fixture defaulted to Detailed; its new
+body now explicitly switches to Simple. The running full suite had already loaded its earlier
+body and records that own failed test. It was not rerun after the design stop. The new connected
+Detailed row-dot test passed. No product design/schema/blueprint/chat/generation/settings/
+template/dependency change was made.
+
+## Attempt checks and other failures
+
+- Focused legend/colour: 5/5 pass, no Docker/database/network.
+- `pnpm check`: 148 files / 1389 tests pass (189.19s); inherited 8 lint warnings/12 infos.
+- Web production build passes; inherited Vite large-chunk warning.
+- Full attempted E2E: 77 pass / 12 fail (6.8m), including both successful mouse rebuilds;
+  exact failures are in `attempt-e2e.log`. Unchanged selector/arrow/dash
+  assertions were never edited. Several mouse line-selection tests fail, and Connect mode’s
+  inline BaseEdge style assertion receives `stroke: transparent; stroke-width: 6.4;` rather
+  than `--board-select`. These remain unresolved, separate from the fatal shared-run premise.
+- Existing PNG route-ink helper reports missing routes. Actual PNG inspection shows routes
+  visibly drawn; the fixed 5×5 centre sample sees the coloured 3.5px stroke (7px at export scale)
+  and can miss its dark outline. This is an inference, not a repaired or accepted result.
+- The first temporary browser harness failed before running because `/tmp/.ts` emitted CJS;
+  switching its own filename to `.mts` fixed that. A later temporary harness’s nested function
+  produced an esbuild `__name` reference in browser evaluation; inlining it fixed the harness.
+  Those tool failures changed no product behavior.
+
+## Partial real browser evidence
+
+The app loaded and TinyURL rendered in Simple/Detailed × light/dark. Each case checked computed
+source tones, async `0.01 12` round beads, one individual soft head per line, selected-tile blue
+outlines and a real mouse wire selection. PNGs were downloaded and decoded; at least four exact
+light tones had more than five pixels. Both views’ PNG bytes are identical between light/dark.
+The first Simple/light PNG was also visually inspected: routes, source colours, beads, dot/fan
+and individual arrowheads are visible in the actual exported image.
+
+Screenshots: [Simple/light](tinyurl-simple-light-matrix.png),
+[Simple/dark](tinyurl-simple-dark-matrix.png),
+[Detailed/light](tinyurl-detailed-light-matrix.png),
+[Detailed/dark](tinyurl-detailed-dark-matrix.png).
+Actual PNGs: [Simple](tinyurl-simple-dark-matrix-export.png),
+[Detailed](tinyurl-detailed-dark-matrix-export.png).
+[Machine outcomes](browser-matrix.json) retain exact tone pixel counts.
+
+YouTube Simple/light rendered and its source tones/beads/individual heads/tile-outline checks
+ran, with [a screenshot](youtube-simple-light-matrix.png), then the chosen wire click failed to
+open its relationship inspector. The larger study’s remaining view/theme cases were not run
+following the fatal design stop. The required complete browser matrix is **not passed**.
+Own browser contexts closed and own browser projects were deleted in `finally`.
+
+## Preservation
+
+Starting own bytes/modes: `/tmp/jeeves-wd06-starting-files.json`.
+All 7256 other byte/mode/absence states match before restoration, including owner changes,
+original apps, historical evidence, accepted SQL/dependencies, frozen v1 and every board file.
+The read-only original RG21 preservation audit passed with process-local `core.abbrev=7`; no
+baseline or Git configuration changed. Original 42 full container triples, 9 networks, 23 volumes,
+43 images and both old E2E rows matched the starting state. Final restored-tree checks and
+preservation are recorded in the appended handoff. No owner 4300/4310 access, branches,
+worktrees, stash, broad staging, push, deployment, paid or live model calls.
